  "articleBody": "Trying to tackle trim repair on your own can seem straightforward, but there are a few common pitfalls that can undermine your efforts. First off, a lot of folks only replace the visibly damaged section without checking for hidden moisture damage. That's a big no-no, as it means the problem will likely pop up again. You've really got to identify the source of any water intrusion, whether it's a leaky gutter or a poorly sealed window, or you're just patching over a recurring issue. Another mistake is skipping those crucial prep steps. We're talking about thorough sanding, applying proper sealants and caulk, and using a good primer. Cutting corners here can drastically shorten the lifespan of your repair, leaving you with peeling paint or new rot much sooner than you'd like. Also, be careful with exterior trim work; make sure you've got a dry weather window, because paint, primer, and sealants need proper curing time. If you're finding these steps overwhelming or suspect hidden issues, that's when calling in a professional like HH Remodeling LLC can save you time and future headaches.",
